# Ending: Ireena given up (strahd_parley is ireena; data/endings/ireena_given_up.json, ADR 0014). With her there the
# party steps aside; without her, they tell him where she is.

~ start
if guest:ireena
-> handed_over
endif
-> told

~ handed_over
Narrator: You step aside. Ireena looks at you once, and then she stops looking at you at all.
Ireena: I am not a coin to be paid over. But I see you have already spent me.
Strahd: Come, my dear. This house has waited a very long time to hear your step.
Narrator: She crosses the hall to him. He offers his arm, she takes it, and the doors close behind them without a sound.
-> after

~ told
Narrator: You tell him where she is. He smiles like a man who already knew, and only wanted to hear you say it.
Strahd: Then I will send my carriage for her tonight. Go home, if you can still remember where that is.
-> after

~ after
if guest:ismark
Ismark: You gave her to him. After everything. Get out of my sight, and out of my village.
endif
Narrator: That night every window in the castle is lit, and music drifts down into the valley. Nobody in Barovia sleeps.
Narrator: The mist does not lift. You have bought your lives, and you will spend them here, under a lord who wants nothing more from you.
-> END
